<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">In the profiles</h2><ul class="yr-prof"><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/wari-empire"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Wari%20Empire.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Wari Empire</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Archaeologists announce an unlooted Wari mausoleum at El Castillo de Huarmey</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/culture/painted-grey-ware-culture"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Painted%20Grey%20Ware%20culture.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Painted Grey Ware culture</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Excavations at Alamgirpur, near Delhi, reveal an overlap between late Harappan and the earliest Painted Grey Ware levels</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/republic-of-egypt"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Republic%20of%20Egypt.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Republic of Egypt</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The military removes President Mohamed Morsi on 3 July; the dispersal of pro-Morsi camps on 14 August kills 595, the deadliest day in modern Egyptian history.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/islamic-republic-of-pakistan"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamic%20Republic%20of%20Pakistan.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamic Republic of Pakistan</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Pakistan Muslim League (N) wins the general election and Nawaz Sharif becomes prime minister for the third time, in the first successful democratic transition.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/empire/oriental-republic-of-uruguay"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Oriental%20Republic%20of%20Uruguay.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Oriental Republic of Uruguay</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">On 11 December Uruguay becomes the first country to fully legalise cannabis, after legalising abortion in 2012 and same-sex marriage in 2013.</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/arab-spring"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Arab%20Spring.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Arab Spring</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">The Egyptian military overthrows Mohamed Morsi, the president elected in 2012</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/social-democracy"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Social%20democracy.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Social democracy</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Most current and former member parties of the Socialist International found the Progressive Alliance</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/ideology/islamism"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Islamism.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Islamism</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A coup deposes Mohamed Morsi of the Muslim Brotherhood, Egypt’s first democratically elected president</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/life/nelson-mandela"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Nelson%20Mandela.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Nelson Mandela</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Mandela dies at his home in Houghton at the age of 95</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/the-communist-manifesto"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/The%20Communist%20Manifesto.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>The Communist Manifesto</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A manuscript page is added to UNESCO's Memory of the World International Register</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/work/gutenberg-bible"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Gutenberg%20Bible.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Gutenberg Bible</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">A copy stolen from Moscow State University in 2009 is recovered in an FSB sting operation</span></li><li><a class="yr-prof-n" href="/movement/mau-mau-rebellion"><img class="pcard-logo" src="/logos/thumbs/Mau%20Mau%20rebellion.png" alt="" width="28" height="28" loading="lazy"><span>Mau Mau rebellion</span></a><span class="yr-prof-t">Britain settles with 5,228 claimants for £19.9 million and denies liability</span></li></ul></section>
